cts with low-back dysfunction</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>1991</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>325</fpage><lpage>330</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1827539</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Takala</surname><given-names>EP</given-names></name><name><surname>Korhonen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Viikari-Juntura</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Postural sway and stepping response among working population: reproducibility, long-term stability, and associations with symptoms of the low back</article-title><source>Clin Biomech (Bristol, Avon)</source><year>1997</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>429</fpage><lpage>437</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11415752</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0268-0033(97)00033-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mientjes</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Balance in chronic low back pain patients compared to healthy people under various conditions in upright standing</article-title><source>Clin Biomech (Bristol, Avon)</source><year>1999</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>710</fpage><lpage>716</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10545625</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0268-0033(99)00025-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>O'Sullivan</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Dankaerts</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Burnett</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Straker</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bargon</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>